## Incremental builds

Microbenchmarks are configured through Python. This means, every time we alter a benchmark
(e.g. test a different patch size), we have to regenerate the Python code and recompile.
A complete ExaHyPE recompile can be expensive. Fortunately, the API offers a make call on
the Peano project, which only builds the files that have actually changed and then links 
